<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#columbian-exchange">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Columbian exchange</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as New World crops</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Columbian Exchange is the transfer of plants, animals, diseases and people between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> and the rest of the world following <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a>'s voyages from 1492. American crops such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maize">maize</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potato">potatoes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassava">cassava</a> transformed nutrition worldwide, while Old World diseases devastated indigenous populations. It was a major consequence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>, and New World crops supported population growth in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>.</p></div>
